  "body": "Replace the implementation-defined choice in *select an image source from a source set* with deterministic selection matching implementations: deduplicate equal pixel densities keeping the earliest entry, sort ascending by pixel density, and pick the first candidate whose pixel density is greater than or equal to the document's device pixel ratio (or the last candidate if none qualify), with a \"may\" allowance for preferring an already-available higher-density candidate.\n\nThis PR reflects current behavior, and we can later reason about making the \"MAY\" part required/interoperable or changing the selection algorithm.\n\nAlso pass the document from `preload` links and return early if no source is selected.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64665.\n\nFixes #13077.\n\n---\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Chromium (already shipped; author of #13077)\n   * Gecko (already implements matching behavior)\n   * WebKit (already implements matching candidate selection; zoom scaling tracked separately)\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/64665\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: N/A (already matches)\n   * Gecko: N/A (already matches)\n   * WebKit: https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=301807 (existing issue)\n- [x] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: N/A\n- [x] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed:\n   * https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46377\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13183/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:42 PM UTC (0516035)\">/images.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13183/01f5b54...0516035/images.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:42 PM UTC (0516035)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13183/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:42 PM UTC (0516035)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13183/01f5b54...0516035/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:42 PM UTC (0516035)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13183/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:42 PM UTC (0516035)\">/links.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13183/01f5b54...0516035/links.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 5, 2026, 1:42 PM UTC (0516035)\">diff</a> )",
